From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 02:35:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: name the iOS virtual monitor \\.\DISPLAY1

With no display sources, GetMonitorInfo named the virtual monitor
"WinDisc", while NtUserEnumDisplayDevices synthesizes one adapter,
\\.\DISPLAY1. Unity 5.5's player builds its display list from
EnumDisplayDevices and finds its window's monitor in it by szDevice; it
found none, so a fullscreen SetResolution sized the window and the
swap chain 0x0:

  NtUserEnumDisplaySettings device L"WinDisc", index 0xffffffff
  AdjustWindowRectEx ((0,0)-(0,0)) 84000000 0 00000000
  D3D11: Failed to create RenderTexture (0 x 0 fmt 19 aa 2)

and Soccer Online: Ball 3D never presented (and wrote 0x0 into its
PlayerPrefs). The same files under desktop Proton, at 1280x720, name the
monitor \\.\DISPLAY1 and size the window 1280x720. The virtual monitor
is now \\.\DISPLAY1, the name of the adapter it is listed under.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-09-ball3d-monitor-name.md
Offered-upstream: no; the synthesized display devices exist only on the iOS port
---
 build/win32u-unix/sysparams_ios.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/win32u-unix/sysparams_ios.c b/build/win32u-unix/sysparams_ios.c
index 49699a5..f72676d 100644
--- a/build/win32u-unix/sysparams_ios.c
+++ b/build/win32u-unix/sysparams_ios.c
@@ -2491,7 +2491,14 @@ static void monitor_get_info( struct monitor *monitor, MONITORINFO *info, struct
     {
         char buffer[CCHDEVICENAME];
         if (monitor->source) snprintf( buffer, sizeof(buffer), "\\\\.\\DISPLAY%d", monitor->source->id + 1 );
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+        /* The virtual monitor is the adapter NtUserEnumDisplayDevices
+         * synthesizes, \\.\DISPLAY1: a game that finds its window's
+         * monitor in that list by name must find it there. */
+        else strcpy( buffer, "\\\\.\\DISPLAY1" );
+#else
         else strcpy( buffer, "WinDisc" );
+#endif
         asciiz_to_unicode( ((MONITORINFOEXW *)info)->szDevice, buffer );
     }
 }
